  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "Preheat oven to 375°F.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash, dry, quarter, and core apples; thinly slice. Place in a 9-inch ovenproof skillet along with frozen cherries, sugar, flour, and cinnamon, then stir to combine the filling.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "4 cups frozen cherries\n¾ cup granulated sugar\n¼ cup all-purpose flour\n½ tsp cinnamon, ground"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Carefully lay pie crust over the filling, crimping the edges as desired. (Depending how deep your skillet is, either drape the pie crust over the skillet edge or fit the pastry fully inside the skillet.) Cut a few slits in the center of the pastry to allow steam to vent. Brush the pastry with milk, then sprinkle with sugar. \n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 (9-inch) “unroll and bake” pie crust\n1 tbsp whole milk\ngranulated sugar"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place skillet in the oven (it doesn't have to be fully heated) and bake until the crust is golden and filling is bubbling, about 1 hour 20 minutes. (Place an aluminum foil-lined baking sheet pan on the rack under the skillet to catch any juice that bubbles over.) Remove from oven and set aside to cool slightly, 20 min.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "To serve, divide pie between plates or bowls and enjoy!",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
